.TH "PKGSOURCE_CODEC" "3" "" "libpkgsource 3.0.0" "libpkgsource"
.SH NAME
pkgsource_codec \- encode canonical durable source\-authority records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include <libpkgsource\-codec/libpkgsource\-codec.h>

pkgsource::codec::profile_catalog_encoding
pkgsource::codec::encode_profile_catalog(
    const pkgsource::profile_catalog& catalog);

pkgsource::profile_catalog pkgsource::codec::decode_profile_catalog(
    const pkgsource::codec::profile_catalog_encoding& encoding);

pkgsource::codec::source_snapshot_encoding
pkgsource::codec::encode_source_snapshot(
    const pkgsource::source_snapshot& snapshot);

pkgsource::source_snapshot pkgsource::codec::decode_source_snapshot(
    const pkgsource::codec::source_snapshot_encoding& encoding);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]libpkgsource\-codec\f[R] is the durable\-record sibling of \f[CR]libpkgsource\f[R].
It owns canonical schema\-one encodings for complete sealed profile catalogs and source snapshots.
.PP
Records use fixed eight\-byte magics, big\-endian integers, bounded length\-prefixed fields, explicit tags, and a final SHA\-256 checksum.
Profile records are limited to 64 MiB, source records to 128 MiB, and each encoded collection to 1,000,000 items.
.PP
\f[CR]decode_profile_catalog()\f[R] reconstructs direct profile declarations and invokes \f[CR]pkgsource::profile_catalog::seal()\f[R].
Stored profile identities must match recomputed identities.
.PP
\f[CR]decode_source_snapshot()\f[R] reconstructs the exact retained profile closure and one complete recipe declaration, then invokes \f[CR]pkgsource::seal_source()\f[R].
The stored source identity must match the recomputed identity.
.PP
Both decoders require canonical byte\-for\-byte re\-encoding.
A checksum\-valid alternate representation, trailing field, or reordered record is rejected.
.SH ERRORS
\f[CR]pkgsource::codec::codec_error\f[R] reports stable \f[CR]pkgsource::codec::codec_error_code\f[R] values for size refusal, truncation, invalid magic, unsupported version, checksum mismatch, invalid record material, identity mismatch, and noncanonical input.
.SH ABI AND PROTOCOL
The codec ABI is \f[CR]libpkgsource\-codec.so.1\f[R].
The normative byte protocol is \f[CR]docs/protocols/source\-records\-v1.md\f[R].
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]libpkgsource(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_profile(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_recipe(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgsource_snapshot(3)\f[R]
